hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15994","Bahz narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, he said, Abd al-Malik ibn Maysara informed me, he said, I heard Kurdus, he said, a man of the people of Badr informed me, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: That I sit in the like of this gathering is more beloved to me than that I free four slaves."
"15995","Hashim narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysara, he said, I heard Kurdus ibn Qays, who was the storyteller of the common people in Kufa, say, a man of the people of Badr informed me, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: That I sit in the like of this gathering is more beloved to me than that I free four slaves. Shu'ba said: So I said, which gathering does he mean? He said: He was a storyteller."
